    "reason": "evidence sufficient (proxy gate verdict; the open aspects need proposals): The linked PR [ev-81b02fa16464] gives the subject: a new Crossplane CLI command, `crossplane xpkg batch`, ported from the `up` tool. Its changed files [ev-42a83e124cc5] show it was added as cmd/crank/xpkg/batch.go. The PR also gives the use case: family providers use it to build their smaller providers in parallel batches and push them by reusing `xpkg push`. That covers the open applicability aspect: the change only matters to operators who choose to run the new CLI command, such as family-provider builders moving off `up` [ev-52670c588642]. The change type is added, and nothing in the evidence says existing behaviour breaks. The `xpkg push` refactor is described only as reuse, not as a behaviour change.",
